    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0980" n="876" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d556-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-03-03">3 March 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>486. In reply to insistent questioning at a press conference today I stated that
                    Italian merchant ships and war ships are now being used in our war effort by the
                    Allied Mediterranean command and that some of the Italian ships or substitutes
                    therefor from the British and American tonnage will be allocated to the Soviet
                    Navy to assist in their requirements for their war effort.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d556-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d556-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent via military channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
